\section{Common mistakes}{

\itemize{
\item Reading \code{r_loo} as a reliability. An \code{r_loo} of .98 does not
mean the CI is 98\% reliable; it means a single producer's
removal changed the group mean by 2\%.
\item Treating \verb{$flagged} as "drop these producers". Investigate
first; cross-check with the rcisignal input-side
\code{run_diagnostics()} to rule out response-coding errors.
\item Lowering \code{flag_threshold} below 2 to flag more producers; that
trades real signal for noise. Use \code{flag_method = "mad"}
instead if the SD rule is dominated by outliers.
}
}

